From 993bad8576bd9d49e6512a602f02f40dd1ffec91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:12:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Cover Studio: editorial magazine covers + shared
 editorial grade

- New lib/cover: 4:5 subject-aware crop, editorial muted grade (sharp) with
  film grain, Pango-autofit three-tier type (kicker / hero headline /
  subline) using bundled OFL fonts, sparkle/arrow accents, headline-behind-
  subject compositing with an occlusion guard and text-over fallback
- Subject matte chain: Replicate background remover (latest version,
  COVER_MATTE_MODEL override) -> gpt-image transparent edit with aspect
  padding -> none; only alpha is taken so original pixels stay untouched
- POST /ai/cover (bills one image only when a fresh matte succeeds; reuse
  re-typesets the stored canvas for free) and POST /ai/cover-copy (brand-
  voiced copy writer with public-figure and NMC-style guardrails, always
  answers via a deterministic fallback)
- Output is the existing {version:1, basePath, layers} doc, so every cover
  piece stays movable in the image editor
- "Editorial cover" Look preset (85mm f/1.4 window light, head in the
  upper-middle, anti-plastic finish)
- Same grade applied to every AI video clip in normalizeVideo, behind the
  editorialVideoGrade kill switch; coverStudio kill switch for the studio
- Web: Cover Studio dialog from AI Studio's image result (auto-draft copy,
  paid-then-free iteration, apply to draft)
- Contract-first: openapi.yaml + regenerated orval clients
- Tests: compose, matte, route billing/validation, dialog

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TokVpPNMo195qrJ5PBmXad
